my name is pearl wolfe and i am the lead  singer songwriter for the band peril and  we are an all girl hasidic rock band  from crown heights brooklyn  all of our live concerts are for women  only  i grew up in a hasidic home  so  having a separation of the sexes in  certain places is pretty common  there's a law and judaism for men  not to listen to the singing voice of a  woman who is not an immediate family  member  i would say one of the biggest  misconceptions that people have about  the hasidic community people think that  women are totally oppressed that women  can't be leaders i felt very much  empowered as a woman spending time with  other powerful women and  having time to connect and having our  own space women deserve a space to rock  out  the response from the hasidic community  has been really positive mostly  you know let's let's empower women let's  make something new for women  when fans come over and tell you  i felt so comfortable tonight i felt  like i could dance i felt like i could  be myself or i really felt a powerful  energy being around other women i'm like  okay we're doing something important and  that's really all that matters  you
 

